 "result": "Everything is in `src/tessel/views.py`.\n\n**Turning the class into a view function**\n- `View.to_view_func(name, *class_args, **class_kwargs)` (a classmethod) builds a plain `view(**kwargs)` function.\n- That function instantiates the class and calls `self.run_view(**kwargs)` through `active_app.ensure_sync`. It instantiates per request when `init_every_request` is true, otherwise it reuses one instance.\n- It copies `view_class`, `__name__`, `__doc__`, `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` onto the function (L129-134).\n- It applies any `decorators` before that.\n- You register the result with `app.attach_route_rule(..., view_func=...)`.\n\n**Routing each method to its handler**\n- **`VerbView.__init_subclass__`** (L165):\n  - Sets `cls.methods` automatically.\n  - It merges the base classes' `methods` with the upper-cased names of any `http_method_funcs` the class defines, such as `get` and `post`.\n  - That is what tells the router which HTTP methods the route accepts.\n- **`VerbView.run_view`** (L182):\n  - Looks up `getattr(self, request.method.lower())` and calls it with the URL kwargs.\n  - `HEAD` falls back to `get` if there is no `head` handler.\n  - It asserts if no handler exists.\n\nThe base `View` has no `run_view`, so you either subclass `VerbView` or implement `dispatch_request`/`run_view` yourself.",
